# People finder

The official variant lists ministers and senior officials. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/finder/people-finder/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

A household rarely needs a public people directory. Where a private installation includes users or responsible contacts, use HA’s existing account and permission management. A reference list may describe roles without publishing personal details.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep the collection scope next to the search label. Use a result title, a short distinguishing description and only the metadata needed for the next decision. The selected criteria and result count should remain visible. A no-match result needs a clear way to broaden the query; an unavailable data source needs a different message.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not reproduce a government office hierarchy or expose presence, location, email addresses or account permissions in a public finder. This template is deliberately limited to role examples. The examples are self-contained specimens with invented records. The second example filters its fixed local list by the words entered, updates the result count, exposes a genuine no-match state and restores all records when cleared. Record details remain readable without JavaScript; submit buttons are disabled until the local handler is ready. No connected search backend or household data is used.

